    "result_text": "Full suite passes: **52 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain email blocklist in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the controller handling `POST /api/owners` where all owner business rules live).\n\nTwo changes, both scoped to the existing email-validation path:\n\n1. Added a `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` set constant with `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, and `guerrillamail.com`.\n2. Extended `normalizeEmail(...)` so that after the existing syntactic check and lower-casing, it extracts the domain (part after `@`) and throws `InvalidRequestException(List.of(\"email\"))` \u2014 which maps to **400 Bad Request** \u2014 when the domain is on the blocklist.\n\nThe check runs on the lower-cased address, so it's case-insensitive, and it only applies when an email is provided (blank/absent email still returns `null` as before). The new `Cp38Tests` acceptance test passes and no existing tests regressed.",
